# Navigation order for the subject taxonomy -- see about/our-taxonomy.md.
# Without this, awesome-pages sorts alphabetically and opens the site on
# christian-life, scattering the doctrinal teaching order.
# salvation is defined in the taxonomy but has no content yet; add it here when
# its directory is created.
nav:
  - index.md
  - scripture
  - god
  - jesus
  - biblical-figures
  - spiritual-beings
  - sin
  - israel-and-church
  - last-things
  - feasts
  - christian-life
  - commentaries
  - sermons
  - resources
  # The two Astro-served tools. They are not mkdocs pages -- they are stitched into the built
  # site by the deploy workflow -- so awesome-pages renders these as plain Links (any nav entry
  # with a title whose value isn't a known file becomes one, with no build warning).
  # Site-absolute paths are required, same as mkdocs.yml's `copyright` link and for the same
  # reason. Site-absolute means from the domain ROOT -- the site is served at the root of
  # the-way.lewy.au, so there is no '/bible_studies' prefix; these carried one until 2026-08-23
  # and 404'd on the live site. Consequence: under `mkdocs serve` they 404 anyway, because the
  # Astro tools aren't running there (`npm run dev` in app/ serves them at :4321).
  # Deliberately flat rather than nested under a "Tools" section: the theme's navigation.prune
  # feature renders a section that is never on the active path as one link to its first child,
  # which would have hidden the genealogy viewer entirely.
  - Prophetic Timeline: /timeline/
  - Genealogy Viewer: /genealogy/
  - about
